<script>
import { url } from '@abide/abide'
import getTeamCommissionSource from 'crm/src/account/getTeamCommission.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import TeamCommission from 'crm/src/account/lib/TeamCommission.abide'
import teamCommissionSource from 'crm/src/account/lib/TeamCommission.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import teamCommissionTestSource from 'crm/src/account/lib/TeamCommission.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import getArchivedDealSource from 'crm/src/pipeline/archive/getArchivedDeal.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import archiveLayoutSource from 'crm/src/pipeline/archive/layout.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import reopenDealSource from 'crm/src/pipeline/archive/reopenDeal.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import ArchivedDeal from 'crm/src/pipeline/lib/ArchivedDeal.abide'
import archivedDealSource from 'crm/src/pipeline/lib/ArchivedDeal.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import archivedDealTestSource from 'crm/src/pipeline/lib/ArchivedDeal.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="`requireRole` lets only an admin read a figure">
        <Example
            id="require-role"
            title="`requireRole(role)` — the team's commission, for admins"
            summary="The whole team's commission this quarter. Maya is an admin and reads it; Theo is in sales and is refused, and so is nobody signed in."
            files={{
                'src/account/lib/TeamCommission.abide': teamCommissionSource,
                'src/account/getTeamCommission.handler.ts': getTeamCommissionSource,
                'src/account/lib/TeamCommission.test.ts': teamCommissionTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <TeamCommission />
        </Example>

        <p>Name the rung in the handler's <code>middleware</code>, and the handler's own body only
            ever runs for an admin. <code>requireRole('admin')</code> reads
            <code>principal.resolved</code> and compares its <code>role</code>, which the CRM's
            <code>onPrincipal</code> adds at sign-in, as
            <a href={url('/ambient/principal')}><code>principal</code></a> shows.
            Pass a function in place of the string for any other test of who is asking:
            <code>{"requireRole((member) => member.name === 'Maya Chen')"}</code>.</p>

        <p>Nobody signed in is refused <code>SignedOut</code> at 401 before any role is read, and
            a member without the role is refused <code>Forbidden</code> at 403. The two are typed on
            the handler's failures, so a page narrows them with
            <code>{"getTeamCommission.isError(error, 'Forbidden')"}</code>, and an
            <code>onRefusal</code> watching for 401 asks for a sign-in. A handler any member may read
            takes <code>signedIn</code>, the 401 alone, as the commission behind
            <a href={url('/configuration/hooks')}><code>onRefusal</code></a> does. A test the two
            rungs cannot spell is a rung of your own, which
            <a href={url('/transports/rpc')}>Handlers</a> writes as <code>adminsOnly</code>.</p>

        <p>A rung runs on every call, in process as much as over the wire, so a test calling the
            handler is refused the way a browser is. Each rung reads the principal the request
            already resolved, once per request, and two rungs cost no second resolve.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="`readOnly` closes a route to writes">
        <Example
            id="read-only"
            title="`middleware(readOnly())` — last year's pipeline, archived"
            summary="A deal from last year's pipeline, filed under an archive that answers reads. Reopening it is refused before the handler runs."
            files={{
                'src/pipeline/lib/ArchivedDeal.abide': archivedDealSource,
                'src/pipeline/archive/layout.abide': archiveLayoutSource,
                'src/pipeline/archive/getArchivedDeal.handler.ts': getArchivedDealSource,
                'src/pipeline/archive/reopenDeal.handler.ts': reopenDealSource,
                'src/pipeline/lib/ArchivedDeal.test.ts': archivedDealTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <ArchivedDeal />
        </Example>

        <p>Filed with <code>middleware</code> in a layout's <code>{'<script server>'}</code>, the rung
            runs over every request below that layout's route. A <code>GET</code>, a
            <code>HEAD</code> and an <code>OPTIONS</code> pass, and any other method is refused
            <code>ReadOnly</code> at 403. Filed in the root layout it makes the whole deployment a
            copy to browse, a demo that takes no changes. See <a href={url('/configuration/hooks')}>Hooks</a>.</p>

        <p>List the handlers whose writes stay open in <code>allow</code>:
            <code>{'readOnly({ allow: [signIn, signOut] })'}</code> still lets a visitor sign in.
            A handler is matched by its address, which moves with the file, so a renamed handler is
            still matched.</p>

        <p>The lane is not the handler's own <code>middleware</code>, so its refusal is not typed on
            the handler's failures, and the card checks it with <code>isFailed</code>. Filed at the
            root it refuses the MCP and Claude Code surfaces too, whose every call is a
            <code>POST</code>, reads included.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
